   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "No to both • Reassure patient she is no longer pregnant. Explain that urine pregnancy test can remain positive for up to 2 months after a TOP. • Advise patient she can become pregnant within 2 weeks following TOP and to avoid intercourse for 7 days after TOP. Offer reliable contraception 170. • Assess patient's mental health. If patient been unable to stop worrying in the past 2 weeks, or felt stress/anxiety/low mood 98.",
   "bbox": [
